From: FlaxAdvisors
Subject: Fix ipmid crash on host boot-override enable (uncaught SdBusError)

MonitorIPMIBootOverrideOpt() is the D-Bus match callback for PropertiesChanged
on /xyz/openbmc_project/control/host0/boot (xyz.openbmc_project.Object.Enable).
When the boot one-time override "Enabled" flag is set true it makes two
synchronous setDbusProperty() calls to "xyz.openbmc_project.OOBInventoryConfig"
-- an AMI OOB service that is not present on this platform. sd_bus_call then
throws sdbusplus SdBusError ("org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.ServiceUnknown: The
name is not activatable").

The callback runs inside sd_bus_process(); an uncaught exception propagates
through sd-bus's C dispatch code and terminates ipmid (std::terminate ->
abort, SIGABRT). systemd restarts ipmid and the next boot-override change
aborts it again -> crash loop. Confirmed from two field coredumps.

Wrap the body in try/catch (like GetInitialExtlogConfigs already does) so a
boot-override change can never abort ipmid.

--- a/ipmid-new.cpp
+++ b/ipmid-new.cpp
@@ -973,20 +973,36 @@
 
 void MonitorIPMIBootOverrideOpt(sdbusplus::message::message& msg)
 {
-    std::string interface;
-    std::map<std::string, std::variant<bool>> properties;
-    auto bus = sdbusplus::bus::new_default();
+    // This is a D-Bus signal match callback invoked from inside sd_bus_process.
+    // Any exception that escapes it propagates through sd-bus's C dispatch code
+    // (which is not exception-safe) and terminates ipmid (std::terminate ->
+    // abort). The serviceOOBInventoryConfig ("xyz.openbmc_project.OOBInventoryConfig")
+    // is an AMI OOB component that is not present on this platform, so the
+    // setDbusProperty() calls below throw sdbusplus SdBusError (ServiceUnknown /
+    // "not activatable") whenever the host boot-override Enabled flag is set.
+    // Catch and log so a boot-override change can never abort ipmid.
+    try
+    {
+        std::string interface;
+        std::map<std::string, std::variant<bool>> properties;
+        auto bus = sdbusplus::bus::new_default();
 
-    msg.read(interface, properties);
-    if (properties.find("Enabled") != properties.end() &&
-        (std::get<bool>(properties["Enabled"])))
+        msg.read(interface, properties);
+        if (properties.find("Enabled") != properties.end() &&
+            (std::get<bool>(properties["Enabled"])))
+        {
+            ipmi::setDbusProperty(bus, serviceOOBInventoryConfig,
+                                  objPathMotherboard, interfaceControlBootOrder,
+                                  propertyBootSourceOverrideEnabled, "Disabled");
+            ipmi::setDbusProperty(bus, serviceOOBInventoryConfig, objPathOobCrc,
+                                  interfaceOobBiosConfigInventoryOobCrc,
+                                  propertyBootOverride, static_cast<uint64_t>(0));
+        }
+    }
+    catch (const std::exception& e)
     {
-        ipmi::setDbusProperty(bus, serviceOOBInventoryConfig,
-                              objPathMotherboard, interfaceControlBootOrder,
-                              propertyBootSourceOverrideEnabled, "Disabled");
-        ipmi::setDbusProperty(bus, serviceOOBInventoryConfig, objPathOobCrc,
-                              interfaceOobBiosConfigInventoryOobCrc,
-                              propertyBootOverride, static_cast<uint64_t>(0));
+        lg2::error("MonitorIPMIBootOverrideOpt: ignoring D-Bus error: {ERROR}",
+                   "ERROR", e.what());
     }
 }
 
